==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Clops Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lightning Li'l Clops Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is ''useless by design''. This Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves. Note that unlike the similar [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this form recharges too slowly to be used as a meatshield.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Li'l Clops Cat essentially serves as an anti-Traitless version of [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Thor Cat]] with similar stats and similar pitfalls. This role is pretty valuable if you manage to obtain it early on, considering the lack of anti-Traitless options at that point in the game. At level 30, it has 36,720 HP against Traitless enemies, which is enough to hold its own against early-game threats like [[R.Ost]] and [[Master A.]], though you should beware that it has 2 knockbacks and no immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s or Crowd-Control effects. Li'l Clops also has a notably longer than average recharge and can be quite expensive to spam with its 540¢ cost.

Beware that while Li'l Clops Cat is a somewhat decent meatshield, especially in {{4c}} or [[Castle & Dragon Collaboration Event#Castle Dragon VS Castle Dragon|Castle Dragon VS Castle Dragon]], you do need to spend real money to obtain it, which is not ideal because of the fact it gets outclassed later on. Once either [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] or [[Brainwashed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Wall Cat]] are obtained, there is little need for this unit.

==='''True Form'''===
The True Form doesn't change much about this unit, the Savage Blow ability doesn't do much other than increasing its effective DPS by roughly 50%. The flaws present in the previous form still apply, meaning Li'l Clops remains niche.

